def enrich(tools,guides):
 tools.extend([
 ('image-converter','Image converter','Images','⇄','Convert between JPG, PNG and WebP, with control over JPEG background color.','Choose a JPG, PNG or WebP image, select the output format and process the image. Dimensions stay the same. JPEG does not support transparency: choose the background color that should replace transparent pixels. PNG ignores the quality setting.','Convert a transparent PNG logo to JPG with a white background, or convert a WebP image to PNG to preserve transparency.','Does changing the file extension convert an image?','No. This tool decodes the source and creates a new image in the selected format. Original metadata is typically removed. Animated images and HEIC, PDF, SVG and AVIF input are not supported.'),
 ('final-grade-calculator','Final grade calculator','Calculators','A?','Find the exam score you need to reach your target course grade.','Enter your current grade excluding the final, your target course grade and the final exam’s percentage weight. Required exam score = (target − current × (1 − weight)) ÷ weight, where weight is written as a decimal. This assumes the final is the only ungraded component.','Current grade 82%, target 85%, final weight 30%: you need 92% on the final.','What if the required score is over 100%?','The target is not reachable with an ordinary 0–100% final under these assumptions. A score at or below zero means the target is already met mathematically, but attendance, minimum-exam marks and other syllabus rules may still apply.')])
 updated=[]
 for t in tools:
  if t[0]=='json-formatter':t=(t[0],t[1],t[2],t[3],'Format, validate and minify JSON while preserving large-number digits.', 'Paste JSON and choose Format or Minify. The browser validates syntax, then a token-preserving formatter changes whitespace only outside strings. Large numbers, decimal notation, escape sequences, property order and duplicate keys are retained. The output does not depend on JavaScript’s rounded numeric values.', 'The identifier 9007199254740993123 remains exactly 9007199254740993123 in the output.', 'Are large numbers and duplicate keys preserved?', 'Yes. Number tokens and key order are preserved, including repeated keys. Repeated keys can still be interpreted differently by downstream software. Standard JSON comments and trailing commas are rejected; files above 2 MB are not supported.')
  if t[0]=='image-resizer':t=(*t[:5],t[5].replace('Output is a static PNG and may be larger than the original file.','Choose JPG, PNG or WebP output. JPEG uses a white background for transparency. PNG output is lossless for the resized pixels and may be larger than the original.'),*t[6:])
  updated.append(t)
 tools[:]=updated
 priorities=['compress-image-to-size','image-resizer','image-converter','image-compressor','word-counter','case-converter','duplicate-line-remover','final-grade-calculator','weighted-grade-calculator','gpa-calculator','percentage-calculator','aspect-ratio-calculator','json-formatter','url-encoder','password-generator']
 tools.sort(key=lambda t:priorities.index(t[0]))
 guides.extend([
 ('what-do-i-need-on-my-final','What grade do I need on my final exam?','Calculators','Turn a target course grade into a specific exam score.',[
 ('Check what your current grade includes','Use the average for completed coursework, excluding the final. A learning platform may show a current average or an overall grade that already treats missing work as zero. Those are different inputs. Confirm the grading display and the final’s percentage weight in your syllabus.'),
 ('Work through the formula','Suppose your completed-work average is 82%, the final is worth 30%, and your target is 85%. Completed work contributes 82 × 0.70 = 57.4 percentage points. The final must contribute 85 − 57.4 = 27.6. Divide by 0.30: you need 92% on the final.'),
 ('Compare a few possible scores','With the same 82% current average and 30% final weight, a final score of 70% gives 78.4% overall, 80% gives 81.4%, and 90% gives 84.4%. The calculator shows these what-if results without assuming what letter grade each percentage represents.'),
 ('Respect local grading rules','Schools in the US, UK, Canada and Australia use different grading structures, and policies vary within each country. A percentage calculation does not determine a letter grade, degree classification or official GPA conversion. Minimum exam marks and compulsory participation can override the simple average.')],['final-grade-calculator','weighted-grade-calculator','gpa-calculator']),
 ('webp-to-jpg-without-upload','Convert WebP or PNG to JPG without uploading','Images','Create a real JPEG file and decide what happens to transparent pixels.',[
 ('A rename is not a conversion','Changing .webp to .jpg changes a filename. It does not change the encoded image data. A proper conversion decodes the source and re-encodes it in the output format. The converter offers a downloadable file using the format the browser actually produced.'),
 ('Choose the transparency background','JPEG cannot represent transparency. A transparent logo needs a solid background when converted to JPEG. Choose a background color in the image converter. For a transparent output, use PNG or WebP instead. Inspect the edges of logos and text before using the result.'),
 ('Use JPEG quality carefully','A quality setting of 80 is a starting point for comparison, not a guarantee of visual quality or a specific file size. Repeated lossy conversions can degrade detail. Keep the source, export once where possible, and compare the result at the size people will actually view it.'),
 ('Know the browser export limits','This converter accepts static JPG, PNG and WebP images, up to 20 MB and 25 million decoded pixels. It does not promise animation, original metadata or color-profile preservation. If an output format is unsupported by the browser, check the actual exported format shown in the result.')],['image-converter','image-compressor','image-resizer']),
 ('format-json-with-large-numbers','Format JSON without rounding large numbers','Developer','Keep identifiers, decimal spelling and escapes unchanged while adjusting layout.',[
 ('Why identifiers can change','JavaScript numbers use binary floating-point arithmetic. Integers beyond 9,007,199,254,740,991 cannot all be represented exactly. Parsing a long identifier into a JavaScript number and serializing it again can therefore change its digits. A formatter should not silently modify an identifier merely to indent its file.'),
 ('Change layout rather than values','Toolnest validates JSON syntax, then emits the original tokens with new whitespace outside strings. For example, 9007199254740993123 stays unchanged. The tokens 1.0, 1e400 and escaped string text also retain their original spelling. This does not make those numbers safe for every downstream parser.'),
 ('Check repeated keys separately','An object may contain repeated keys. Toolnest preserves them and their order. Many parsers keep only the last value, so preserving the text does not resolve ambiguity in the data. Review repeated keys before using the result in production systems.'),
 ('Use safe inputs and verify outputs','Paste only data you are authorized to process. This tool does not upload the input or execute it as code. It accepts standard JSON without comments or trailing commas, with a 2 MB input limit. Keep the original and check how the receiving application interprets its numbers.')],['json-formatter','url-encoder','duplicate-line-remover'])])
